# Saturday June 13 2026 — Morning Session Notes

## Python Functions
- def keyword defines a function
- Calling a function is what makes it run
- Parameters go inside the parentheses
- Definition always comes before the call
- Example: def check_device(device):

## Linux File Permissions
- ls -la shows files with permission strings
- Format: -rwxrwxr-x
- Position 1: file type (- = file, d = directory)
- Position 2-4: owner permissions
- Position 5-7: group permissions
- Position 8-10: other users permissions
- r = read, w = write, x = execute

## chmod Commands
- chmod +x filename = add execute permission
- chmod -x filename = remove execute permission
- chmod 755 filename = owner rwx, group r-x, other r-x
- chmod 644 filename = owner rw-, group r--, other r--

## chown Command
- chown kris:kris filename = change owner and group
- Needed when root creates a file you need to edit

## Navigation Review
- cd ~/Vanguard-lab = go to lab from anywhere
- cd foldername = go into subfolder
- ls -la = list files with permissions
- ./ = run executable file directly
- && = chain commands, second runs if first succeeds

## Key Terms
- Parameter = variable inside a function definition
- Iteration variable = the item in a for loop
- Execute permission = ability to run a file directly

